#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:9
msgid "Installing MVSim on Ubuntu - tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:12
msgid ""
"MVSim provides lightweight mobile robot simulation with native integration "
"for ROS topics and messages. This tutorial shows how to install MVSim on "
"Ubuntu from binary packages or source and verify the installation. After "
"following it, you will be ready to launch MVSim demos and build custom "
"worlds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:20
msgid "**Goal:** Install the ``mvsim`` package on Ubuntu and verify it works."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:22
msgid "**Tutorial level:** Advanced"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:24
msgid "**Time:** 10 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:28
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:31
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:33
msgid ""
"`MVSim <https://mvsimulator.readthedocs.io/>`__ (MultiVehicle Simulator) is "
"a lightweight, open-source simulator for mobile robots. It provides 2D "
"physics-based simulation with 3D visualization, supporting differential "
"drive and Ackermann vehicles, multiple sensor types (LiDAR, cameras, IMU, "
"GPS), and native ROS 2 integration via standard message types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:37
msgid "MVSim is licensed under the BSD 3-clause license."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:40
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:42
msgid ""
"It is recommended to understand basic ROS principles covered in the beginner "
"tutorials. In particular, :doc:`../../../ROS-Framework/client-libraries/"
"Working-with-Client-Libraries/Creating-A-Workspace/Creating-A-Workspace` is "
"a useful prerequisite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:45
msgid ""
"You should have a working ROS 2 installation. Follow the :doc:`ROS 2 install "
"instructions <../../../Get-Started/Installation>` if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:49
msgid "Tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:52
msgid "1 Install ``mvsim``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:54
msgid ""
"You can either install the released binary package or build from sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:58
msgid "Install from ROS binary packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:60
msgid "Run the following command in a terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:62
msgid "$ sudo apt install ros-rolling-mvsim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:66
msgid "Build from sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:68
msgid "Create a ROS 2 workspace if you don't already have one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:70
msgid "$ mkdir -p ~/ros2_ws/src"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:74
msgid "Source the ROS 2 environment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:76
msgid "$ source /opt/ros/rolling/setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:80
msgid "Clone the MVSim repository:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:82
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros2_ws/src\n"
"$ git clone https://github.com/MRPT/mvsim.git --recursive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:87
msgid "Install dependencies using ``rosdep``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:89
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros2_ws\n"
"$ rosdep install --from-paths src --ignore-src -r -y"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:94
msgid "Build the package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:96
msgid ""
"$ colcon build --symlink-install --cmake-args -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:100
msgid "Source the workspace:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:102
msgid "$ source install/setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:107
msgid "2 Verify the installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:109
msgid "Check that the ``mvsim`` CLI is available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:111
msgid "$ mvsim --version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:115
msgid "You should see the installed version number printed to the terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:119
msgid "The ``mvsim`` package provides two executables:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:121
msgid "``mvsim``: the main CLI tool for running the simulator standalone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:122
msgid ""
"``mvsim_node``: a ROS 2 node wrapper for running the simulator and connect "
"it to other ROS 2 nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:125
msgid "3 Launch a demo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:127
msgid ""
"To quickly verify everything is working, launch the warehouse demo with ROS "
"2:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:129
msgid "$ ros2 launch mvsim demo_warehouse.launch.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:133
msgid ""
"You should see the MVSim GUI window open with a Jackal robot in a warehouse "
"environment. Use the keyboard (W/A/S/D keys) to drive the robot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:137
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/MVSim/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:139
msgid ""
"You have installed MVSim and verified it works by launching a demo world. In "
"the next tutorial, you will learn how to launch different demo scenarios and "
"interact with them through ROS 2 topics."
msgstr ""
